.Dd $Mdocdate$
.Dt d2 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm d2
.Nd compiles and renders d2 diagrams into svgs.
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm d2
.Op Fl -watch Ar false
.Op Fl -theme Em 0
.Op Fl -salt Ar string
.Ar file.d2
.Op Ar file.svg | file.png | file.pdf | file.pptx | file.gif | file.txt
.Nm d2
.Ar layout Op Ar name
.Nm d2
.Ar fmt Ar file.d2 ...
.Nm d2
.Ar play Ar file.d2
.Nm d2
.Ar validate Ar file.d2
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
compiles and renders
.Ar file.d2
to
.Ar file.svg
|
.Ar file.png
|
.Ar file.pdf
|
.Ar file.pptx
|
.Ar file.gif
|
.Ar file.txt
.Ns .
.Pp
It defaults to
.Ar file.svg
if no output path is passed.
.Pp
Pass - to have
.Nm
read from stdin or write to stdout.
.Pp
PNG exports support up to 32768 pixels per dimension, subject to rendering resource limits.
.Pp
Never use the presence of the output file to check for success.
Always use the exit status of
.Nm d2
.Ns .
This is because sometimes when errors occur while rendering, d2 still write out a partial
render anyway to enable iteration on a broken diagram.
.Pp
See more docs, the source code and license at
.Lk https://github.com/d2lang/d2
.Ns .
.Pp
Hosted icons at
.Lk https://icons.d2lang.com
.Ns .
.Pp
Playground runner at
.Lk https://play.d2lang.com
.Ns .
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Fl
.It Fl w , -watch Ar false
Watch for changes to input and live reload. Use
.Ev $PORT and Ev $HOST to specify the listening address.
.It Fl h , -host Ar localhost
Host listening address when used with
.Ar watch
.Ns .
.It Fl p , -port Ar 0
Port listening address when used with
.Ar watch
.Ns .
.It Fl t , -theme Ar 0
Set the diagram theme ID
.Ns .
.It Fl -dark-theme Ar -1
The theme to use when the viewer's browser is in dark mode. When left unset
.Fl -theme
is used for both light and dark mode. Be aware that explicit styles set in D2 code will
still be applied and this may produce unexpected results. We plan on resolving this by
making style maps in D2 light/dark mode specific. See
.Lk https://github.com/d2lang/d2/issues/831
.Ns .
.It Fl s , -sketch Ar false
Renders the diagram to look like it was sketched by hand
.Ns .
.It Fl -isometric Ar false
Render SVG, PNG, GIF, PDF or PPTX with the native Go isometric renderer.
Preserve compiled positions and dimensions, and render nested source containers as platforms.
Like sketch, this can also be enabled using D2_ISOMETRIC=true or
vars: {d2-config: {isometric: true}} in D2 source.
An explicit flag takes precedence over the environment, which takes precedence over source config.
Use --isometric=false to disable a source or environment setting.
Without an output filename, --isometric defaults to SVG.
No browser or GPU is required.
Images fit the diagram within 1600 by 1000 pixels, or 1000 by 625 pixels for
GIF, with a fixed camera. Use --scale to change those maximum dimensions.
A single-board GIF uses an 8.33-second traffic cycle, or an 8-second
cycle when it includes animated shapes or source panels, so both loop cleanly.
Authored style.animated enables motion.
Multiple boards export to SVG or PNG directories, PDF pages, PPTX slides or one GIF slideshow, in root,
layers, scenarios, steps order. Folder-only boards are skipped.
PDF and PPTX preserve board navigation and clickable source links.
Their pages embed the same native image as PNG export, with projected link regions.
GIF slides default to 1000ms per board; --animate-interval changes that delay.
Use --target to select a board or --target='' for the root without subboards.
Cannot be combined with sketch or force-appendix. Isometric SVG currently rejects dark-theme
and animated multi-board SVG; use separate themed SVGs or a GIF slideshow.
.Ns .
.It Fl -center Ar flag
Center the SVG in the containing viewbox, such as your browser screen
.Ns .
.It Fl -scale Ar -1
Scale the output. E.g., 0.5 to halve the default size. Default -1 means that SVG's will fit to screen and all others will use their default render size. Setting to 1 turns off SVG fitting to screen
.Ns .
.It Fl -font-regular
Path to .ttf file to use for the regular font. If none provided, Source Sans Pro Regular is used
.Ns .
.It Fl -font-italic
Path to .ttf file to use for the italic font. If none provided, Source Sans Pro Regular-Italic is used
.Ns .
.It Fl -font-bold
Path to .ttf file to use for the bold font. If none provided, Source Sans Pro Bold is used
.Ns .
.It Fl -font-semibold
Path to .ttf file to use for the semibold font. If none provided, Source Sans Pro Semibold is used
.Ns .
.It Fl -font-mono
Path to .ttf file to use for the monospace font. If none provided, Source Code Pro Regular is used
.Ns .
.It Fl -font-mono-bold
Path to .ttf file to use for the monospace bold font. If none provided, Source Code Pro Bold is used
.Ns .
.It Fl -font-mono-italic
Path to .ttf file to use for the monospace italic font. If none provided, Source Code Pro Italic is used
.Ns .
.It Fl -font-mono-semibold
Path to .ttf file to use for the monospace semibold font. If none provided, Source Code Pro Semibold is used
.Ns .
.It Fl -pad Ar 100
Pixels padded around the rendered diagram
.Ns .
.It Fl -animate-interval Ar 0
Set the time each board is displayed in an animated SVG or GIF. The flag takes milliseconds.
Set the same interval in D2 source with
.Li "vars: {d2-config: {animate-interval: 800ms}}" .
The source value accepts integer milliseconds or a duration such as 1.5s.
The flag takes precedence over D2_ANIMATE_INTERVAL, which takes precedence over the file.
Zero selects ordinary SVG export or the default GIF interval of 1000ms.
.Ns .
.It Fl -browser Ar true
Browser executable that watch opens. Setting to 0 opens no browser
.Ns .
.It Fl l , -layout Ar dagre
Set the diagram layout engine to the passed string. For a list of available options, run
.Ar layout
.Ns .
.It Fl -elk-algorithm Ar algorithm
Select the ELK layout algorithm. The default is layered.
Other choices for connected diagrams are force, stress, mrtree and radial.
.It Fl -elk-forceModel Ar model
Use the fruchterman_reingold (default) or eades force model.
.It Fl -elk-forceRepulsion Ar strength
Set repulsion between unconnected nodes in the eades force model. The default is 5.
.It Fl -elk-stressDesiredEdgeLength Ar distance
Set the target center-to-center distance between connected nodes in stress layout. The default is 100.
.It Fl -elk-mrtreeSearchOrder Ar order
Build the spanning tree depth-first (dfs, the default) or breadth-first (bfs).
.It Fl -elk-mrtreeWeighting Ar order
Order sibling branches by model_order (the default), descendants or fan.
.It Fl -elk-radialRadius Ar distance
Set the initial spacing between tree levels in radial layout. The default, 0, chooses it automatically.
.It Fl -elk-radialWedgeCriteria Ar criterion
Divide angular space between radial branches by node_size (the default) or leaf_number.
.It Fl -elk-radialCompactor Ar mode
Pack radial rings with radial_compaction or individual branches with wedge_compaction. The default is none.
.It Fl -elk-nodeNode , -elk-edgeNode , -elk-edgeEdge Ar distance
Minimum spacing between nodes, between edges and nodes, or between edges in the same ELK layer.
.It Fl -elk-edgeRouting Ar style
Route ELK edges with orthogonal or polyline segments.
.It Fl -elk-wrappingStrategy Ar strategy
Wrap a long ELK pipeline with single_edge or multi_edge. The default is off.
.It Fl -elk-forceNodeModelOrder
Preserve the declaration order of nodes within layers at the root of the diagram.
.It Fl -elk-feedbackEdges
Route backward connections around the main flow.
.It Fl -elk-mergeEdges
Share attachment points for ordinary incoming or outgoing edges.
Set these options in a diagram with the flag name inside vars.d2-config.data.
Diagram settings take precedence over the CLI.
Set elk-layer-constraint on a shape to first, last or none.
These option values are case-insensitive.
.It Fl b , -bundle Ar true
Bundle all assets and layers into the output svg
.Ns .
.It Fl -allow-private-network Ar false
Allow remote image assets to access private, loopback, and link-local networks. Only enable this for trusted diagrams
.Ns .
.It Fl -force-appendix Ar false
Add a numbered appendix for tooltips and links to SVG exports, including each frame of an animated SVG. PNG exports include an appendix by default
.Ns .
.It Fl -target
Target board to render. Pass an empty string to target root board. If target ends with '*', it will be rendered
with all of its scenarios, steps, and layers. Otherwise, only the target board will be rendered. E.g. --target=''
to render root board only or --target='layers.x.*' to render layer 'x' with all of its children
.Ns .
.It Fl d , -debug
Print debug logs
.Ns .
.It Fl -img-cache Ar true
In watch mode, images used in icons are cached for subsequent compilations. This should be disabled if images might change
.Ns .
.It Fl -timeout Ar 120
The maximum number of seconds that D2 runs for before timing out and exiting. When rendering a large diagram, it is recommended to increase this value
.Ns .
.It Fl -check Ar false
Check that the specified files are formatted correctly
.Ns .
.It Fl -salt Ar string
Add a salt value to ensure the output uses unique IDs. This is useful when generating multiple identical diagrams to be included in the same HTML doc, so that duplicate id's do not cause invalid HTML. The salt value is a string that will be appended to IDs in the output.
.Ns .
.It Fl h , -help
Print usage information and exit
.Ns .
.It Fl v , -version
Print version information and exit
.Ns .
.It Fl -stdout-format Ar string
Set the output format when writing to stdout. Supported formats are: png, svg, ascii, txt, pdf, pptx, gif. Only used when output is set to stdout (-)
.Ns .
.It Fl -no-xml-tag Ar false
Omit XML tag (<?xml ...?>) from output SVG files. Useful when generating SVGs for direct HTML embedding
.Ns .
.It Fl -omit-version Ar false
omit D2 version from generated image
.Ns .
.It Fl -ascii-mode Ar extended
ASCII rendering mode for text outputs. Options: 'standard' (basic ASCII chars) or 'extended' (Unicode chars)
.Ns .
.El
.Sh SUBCOMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width Fl
.It Ar layout
Lists available layout engine options with short help
.Ns .
.It Ar layout Op Ar name
Display long help for a particular layout engine, including its configuration options
.Ns .
.It Ar themes
Lists available themes
.Ns .
.It Ar fmt Ar file.d2 ...
Format all passed files
.It Ar play Ar file.d2
Opens the file in playground, an online web viewer (https://play.d2lang.com)
.It Ar validate Ar file.d2
Validates file.d2
.El
